From: OpenIRD contributors
Subject: [PATCH] kbuild: let KBUILD_BUILD_USER/HOST name the builder in the banner

The version banner ("Linux version ... (user@host) ...") is filled in from
whoami and hostname, so every build carries the name of whoever built it
and of their machine, and two builds of the same source never match.  This
tree already takes the build time from KBUILD_BUILD_TIMESTAMP; take the
user and the host from KBUILD_BUILD_USER and KBUILD_BUILD_HOST the same
way, falling back to whoami/hostname when they are not set.

scripts/build-kernel.sh sets all three, so an OpenIRD kernel says
"openird@openird" whoever builds it.  Mainline later grew the same two
variables.

Origin: gpl-derived
---
--- a/scripts/mkcompile_h
+++ b/scripts/mkcompile_h
@@ -60,8 +60,8 @@
   echo \#define UTS_VERSION \"`echo $UTS_VERSION | $UTS_TRUNCATE`\"
 
   echo \#define LINUX_COMPILE_TIME \"`date +%T`\"
-  echo \#define LINUX_COMPILE_BY \"`whoami`\"
-  echo \#define LINUX_COMPILE_HOST \"`hostname | $UTS_TRUNCATE`\"
+  echo \#define LINUX_COMPILE_BY \"${KBUILD_BUILD_USER:-`whoami`}\"
+  echo \#define LINUX_COMPILE_HOST \"`echo ${KBUILD_BUILD_HOST:-\`hostname\`} | $UTS_TRUNCATE`\"
 
   if [ -x /bin/dnsdomainname ]; then
     echo \#define LINUX_COMPILE_DOMAIN \"`dnsdomainname | $UTS_TRUNCATE`\"
